/* GENERATED by scripts/gen_wasm_imports.py from the headers of sdk/include/shard : do not edit, change a header or the script and run
 * python scripts/gen_wasm_imports.py (the test Wasm.GeneratedImports checks it is up to date).
 *
 * The module side of a sandboxed plugin (tier 2, "abi": "wasm1") : every function of the interfaces the sandbox offers is an import of the
 * host (module "shard"), named "<interface>.<function>", with the signature Clang gives the C function on wasm32 (a ShardStr by value, and
 * every struct, goes by address). The tables of the C ABI (ShardCVarsApi...) are built from those imports, and the ShardHostApi the plugin
 * is handed is shard_wasm_host_table : the host reads its address from the exported global of that name (wasm-ld --export=shard_wasm_host_table)
 * and passes it to shard_plugin_entry, so a plugin written for the C ABI compiles unchanged for wasm32. See shard_wasm.h. */
